# but keep the spike's reference inputs
!spike/talk.en.vtt

# Reframe ML eval golden set (WU R0) — PRIVATE / third-party, NEVER committed.
# The OpusClip-derived golden reference (the razvan_gandu RO talk-show + its 41
# derived clips) is sourced via the REFRAME_GOLDEN_DIR env var (an EXTERNAL path,
# e.g. ~/Downloads/razvan_gandu); these patterns defend against an accidental
# repo-relative copy. The 100% pure-coverage tier never needs these bytes.
razvan_gandu/
**/razvan_gandu/
testdata/razvan_gandu/

# Local agent / orchestration state (never commit — machine-local recovery)
.beads/
# `.claude/*`, NOT `.claude/` — git cannot re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY
# is excluded, so a trailing-slash directory pattern makes every `!` below inert.
# With `.claude/*` the listed subdirectories are themselves un-excluded, and nothing
# then excludes their contents.
#
# Why this needed narrowing: agent CONFIG is project authority and belongs in the
# repo, but the blanket pattern silently dropped every future file — measured, a
# brand-new `.claude/commands/x.md` resolved to `.gitignore:63` — while six files
# were already tracked and so kept working (gitignore does not affect tracked
# files). That split is invisible until someone adds a command and it never lands.
# Machine-local state (homunculus/, settings.local.json, caches) stays ignored.
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/*.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Mutation-testing artifacts (regenerated by the nightly mutation.yml — never commit)
.mutmut-cache
mutants/
sidecar/mutants/
app/.stryker-tmp/
app/reports/mutation/
stryker.log

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# secrets (cloud key lives in app settings/OS, never the repo)
secrets.local.*
*.secret

# build artifacts (installer + unpacked) — never commit
dist/
# Built installers (NSIS .exe + portable .zip) — large binaries; attach to
# GitHub Releases, never commit to the repo.
installers/

# Regenerable build binaries (staged by build/python-embed-setup.ps1 -WithFfmpeg)
build/ffmpeg/
# The dedicated py3.14 embeddable for the isolated chatterbox env is large and
# regenerable by the same prep script — never commit it (mirrors build/ffmpeg/).
# NOTE: build/python-embed/ (py3.12) IS tracked historically; this only covers 3.14.
build/python-embed-314/
# ...and the name the prep script actually stages into. The rule above only matched
# `-314`, so a 23.6 MB staged interpreter (36 files: python.exe, python312.dll,
# python312.zip, 17 .pyd, get-pip.py) slipped into a checkpoint commit despite the
# stated "never commit it" intent. Nothing in the repo references this directory —
# chatterbox.py materializes its isolated env at %APPDATA%/media-studio/envs/chatterbox
# via assets.ensure(["chatterbox-env"]) + pip --target at RUNTIME, not from the tree.
build/python-embed-chatterbox/
# Stray duplicate icon dir — the REAL app icons live in build/icons/ (plural,
# committed by WU A2). build/icon/ (singular) is a regenerable leftover dup an
# icon step emits; never commit it (the tracked build/icons/ is the source of truth).
build/icon/

# Runtime data root (models/exports/envs — relocatable via MEDIA_STUDIO_CONFIG_DIR)
/data/

# Ad-hoc audit/analysis scratch (agent probe scripts, raw journals, superseded
# ledger intermediates, screenshots). ~10 MB of derived bytes; genuinely disposable,
# and `git clean -xfd` is expected to be safe here.
#
# That safety used to be false: the regeneration recipe for the tracked ledger lived
# in HERE, so cleaning the derived bytes also destroyed the only way to reproduce
# them. Fixed by MOVING the recipe out rather than by carving negations into this
# pattern — the tools are now tracked at `docs/validation/tools/`, one canonical
# home. Un-ignoring them in place would have tracked each in two locations, which is
# the exact duplication this SSOT pass exists to remove.
.audit/

# On-demand functional-sweep output (e2e/audit + playwright.audit.config.ts).
# Findings are transient investigation data; the FIX lands as code + tests, so
# the raw report is never committed.
app/audit-artifacts/

# Transient agent probe scripts. A fan-out agent asked to VERIFY a finding will
# sometimes write a throwaway probe next to the code it is testing (e.g. a Playwright
# control that proves a CSS rule really does defeat [hidden]). That is the executable
# rigor we want, but the files are scratch and must never become commit-eligible --
# a prior wave leaked zz*/__* scratch into app/renderer/src and broke tsc --noEmit.
.tmp-*
**/.tmp-*
